<section class="pagehead">
  <p class="label">About</p>
  <h1 class="pagehead__title">How this works</h1>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="prose" data-reveal>
    <p>
      Travel sites sort by country, by price, or by whatever the affiliate deal
      pays this month. This one sorts by <strong>the hour</strong>. Each of the
      six destinations is filed under the time of day it earns its reputation,
      and the six run in order from just past midnight to just before eight in
      the evening.
    </p>
    <p>
      The background is not a photograph. It is a gradient built from the
      colours of that hour in that place, and it is redrawn on every scroll
      event, interpolating between one destination and the next. The sun moves
      left to right and rises and sets with the list. The clock in the corner
      shows the time you are currently looking at, not the time where you are.
    </p>
    <p>
      Skylines are drawn as flat silhouettes rather than shot on location: a
      caldera edge at Imerovigli, pagoda tiers in Higashiyama, a granite ridge
      in Fiordland. Every destination and every claim about seasons and flights
      is real. The properties are illustrative and nothing here is bookable.
    </p>
    <p>
      Built as a static site with Eleventy, animated with GSAP and Lenis, and
      deployed on Netlify. Motion is disabled entirely when the browser asks
      for reduced motion.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
